#N canvas 0 50 1040 930 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   cross~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 cross synthesis between two sounds;
#X text 30 86 cross synthesis. the left inlet is sound a (the one you hear) and the right inlet is sound b. a takes the spectral shape or phase of b, f 110;
#X text 30 146 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 190 the same stft engine with two inputs. four methods combine the magnitude and phase of the two frames: a spectral envelope vocoder and phase borrowing and magnitude borrowing and a morph, f 110;
#X text 30 250 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 294 1  open the engine page and switch the tones on, f 110;
#X text 30 324 2  choose a method. envelope gives the classic vocoder sound, f 110;
#X text 30 354 3  lower amount to blend sound a back in, f 110;
#X text 30 384 everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy. every effect has presets and a and b morph and mutate and a data inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 444 try:  use a sustained sound as a and speech or drums as b for the best vocoder effect, f 110;
#X text 30 474 try:  morph moves levels and phase from a to b together, f 110;
#X text 30 518 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 562 nothing happens: sound b needs to be connected to the right inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 592 weak effect: raise amount and mix, f 110;
#X text 30 622 names: give every instance its own name as the first argument like [tessera/cross~ c1]. the name is also the stash namespace, f 110;
#X text 30 686 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1026 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 factory sounds are stored as plain text. click a box to load that sound. every slider in the effect follows, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; c1 preset 0;
#X text 240 112 0  default;
#X msg 30 164 \; c1 preset 1;
#X text 240 166 1  vocoder;
#X msg 30 218 \; c1 preset 2;
#X text 240 220 2  coarse vocoder;
#X msg 460 110 \; c1 preset 3;
#X text 670 112 3  phase borrow;
#X msg 460 164 \; c1 preset 4;
#X text 670 166 4  magnitude borrow;
#X msg 460 218 \; c1 preset 5;
#X text 670 220 5  half morph;
#X text 30 292 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 336 20 0 0 0 - c1-name -;
#X floatatom 230 336 4 0 0 0 - c1-index -;
#X text 340 338 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 380 \; c1 next;
#X msg 142 380 \; c1 prev;
#X msg 254 380 \; c1 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 440 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1. mutate leaves mix and level alone, f 100;
#X text 30 490 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 534 \; c1 A;
#X msg 118 534 \; c1 B;
#X text 206 536 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 596 morph;
#X obj 110 594 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 c1-morph empty empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 638 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every continuous parameter blends smoothly. switches change at the middle, f 100;
#X text 30 688 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 732 \; c1 store mysound;
#X msg 214 732 \; c1 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 732 \; c1 load my.bank;
#X text 30 792 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load reads such a file, f 100;
#X text 30 842 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 886 every slider of the effect sends to c1-param and listens on c1-param-r. this is the naming scheme of the stash preset library: create [stash/bank c1] and send it a scan message with the name of the patch that holds the effect. it follows the stash rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 730 pd presets;
#X text 30 764 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1200 394 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every parameter is also a message: [name value( in real units or for a switch the option name or number. the controls in the effect panel and these messages do the same, f 120;
#X text 30 66 parameter;
#X text 210 66 values;
#X text 560 66 what it does;
#X text 30 100 cmode;
#X text 210 100 envelope | phase | magnitude | morph, f 36;
#X text 560 100 envelope phase magnitude or morph, f 54;
#X text 30 156 amount;
#X text 210 156 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 156 0 is a alone and 1 is the full effect, f 54;
#X text 30 192 width;
#X text 210 192 1 to 64, f 36;
#X text 560 192 how coarse the spectral envelope is in the envelope method, f 54;
#X text 30 248 mix;
#X text 210 248 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 248 0 is the dry sound and 1 is only the effect, f 54;
#X text 30 294 any continuous parameter can be driven by data: send datamap name amount and then data 0 to 1. see the messages page, f 120;
#X restore 220 730 pd parameters;
#X text 220 764 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1142 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the effect. the effect listens to its name so you can use [s c1] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X text 30 66 message;
#X text 430 66 what it does;
#X msg 30 100 \; c1 params;
#X text 430 102 prints every parameter and its range in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 154 \; c1 preset 3;
#X text 430 156 loads preset 3 (or a preset by name: preset vocoder), f 76;
#X msg 30 208 \; c1 next;
#X text 430 210 next preset (wraps around), f 76;
#X msg 30 262 \; c1 prev;
#X text 430 264 previous preset, f 76;
#X msg 30 316 \; c1 mutate 0.4;
#X text 430 318 random variation of the current sound. 0 is nothing and 1 is a lot, f 76;
#X msg 30 370 \; c1 A;
#X text 430 372 remember the current sound as a, f 76;
#X msg 30 424 \; c1 B;
#X text 430 426 remember the current sound as b, f 76;
#X msg 30 478 \; c1 morph 0.5;
#X text 430 480 blend between a and b from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 532 \; c1 data 0.7;
#X text 430 534 data inlet: a value from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 586 \; c1 datamap amount 0.5;
#X text 430 588 map the data inlet to a continuous parameter. 0.5 means the full range of the parameter at data 0 and 1. amount 0 removes the mapping. up to four mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 660 \; c1 datamap clear;
#X text 430 662 remove all data mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 714 \; c1 store mysound;
#X text 430 716 keep the current sound in the user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 768 \; c1 save my.bank;
#X text 430 770 write the user bank to a text file, f 76;
#X msg 30 822 \; c1 load my.bank;
#X text 430 824 read a user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 876 \; c1 size 4096;
#X text 430 878 fft size 256 to 16384 (latency equals the size), f 76;
#X msg 30 930 \; c1 reset;
#X text 430 932 clears the buffers, f 76;
#X msg 30 984 \; c1 latency;
#X text 430 986 prints the delay in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 1038 \; c1 cmode phase;
#X text 430 1040 method by name or number, f 76;
#X restore 410 730 pd messages;
#X text 410 764 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1000 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to the effect through [s c1] so the engine page must be open with dsp on, f 130;
